# Tracer: explicit definition failures retain their actual obligation.
#
# Before:
# prop positive(x R):
#     x > 0
# by def $positive(0)
# Former result: DefinitionUnavailable discarded the failed 0 > 0 obligation.
#
# Now: the same negative call remains rejected with phase
# definition_requirement, index 1 (after the parameter-type requirement),
# goal 0 > 0, and the actual rejected verification result.
# The executable negative checks are in src/json_output/error_context_tests.rs
# and tests/integration/cli_feedback.rs. They also check no session termination
# and a subsequent successful call in the same context.
#
# Active positive boundary: supported user and builtin definitions still verify.
prop positive(x R):
    x > 0
by def $positive(1)
by def {1} $proper_subset {1, 2}
#
# Boundary: abstract_prop still has no expandable definition; failed conditions
# remain rejected. Ordinary search retains its original route order and budgets.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -lang en -strict -f examples/stmt_nodes/by/by_def_failure_diagnostics.lit
# Focused negative gate: cargo test --release --lib json_output::error_context_tests
